1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,540
The wind is blowing, but
the turbine is stopped.

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:03,260
Is it broken?

3
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:04,310
Usually, no.

4
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:06,660
If the wind is too weak, there's no power.

5
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:10,880
On this model, for example, the turbine
stops below 3 meters per second,

6
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,530
about 7 miles per hour.

7
00:00:12,630 --> 00:00:14,510
It also stops in very strong wind.

8
00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:18,270
Above 25 meters per second,
about 56 miles per hour,

9
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:19,940
the blades are feathered for safety.

10
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:23,780
At the base of the tower, the answer to
why it stopped is usually not a fault.

11
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:25,370
It's one end of this curve.

12
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:27,810
Turbines are also stopped
for planned maintenance.

13
00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:28,990
The breaker is opened.

14
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:30,370
Then it's locked and tagged.

15
00:00:30,390 --> 00:00:32,540
If required, the rotor lock goes in too.

16
00:00:32,730 --> 00:00:35,390
Sometimes the wind and the
machine are both ready,

17
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:37,690
but the grid operator sends a curtailment,

18
00:00:37,710 --> 00:00:39,050
and the turbine is stopped.

19
00:00:39,070 --> 00:00:40,150
This is not a fault.

20
00:00:40,170 --> 00:00:42,270
If there's an alarm, it's a different job:

21
00:00:42,290 --> 00:00:43,680
read the alarm first.

22
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:45,060
It works the other way too:

23
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:46,980
no wind, but the nacelle is turning.

24
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:47,540
Not the rotor.

25
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:48,850
The nacelle on top.

26
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:52,260
The power cables inside the
tower twist as the nacelle yaws.

27
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:56,800
After a set number of turns, the turbine
turns back the other way to untwist them,

28
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:57,950
wind or no wind.

29
00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:00,340
More from the field at sonersoylu.com.

30
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:01,280
The Turbine Tech.

31
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:02,790
Follow for the next question.
